1
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,540
This is berk,

2
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:17,670
the best kept secret this side of, well...

3
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:19,570
Anywhere.

4
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,310
Granted, it may not look like much,

5
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:22,580
but this wet heap of rock

6
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,810
packs more than a few surprises.

7
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,550
Life here is amazing,

8
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,420
just not for the faint of heart.

9
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:38,430
You see, where most folks enjoy hobbies like whittling

10
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:41,600
or needlepoint, we berkians prefer...

11
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:46,400
...A little something we like to call...

12
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:51,240
...dragon racing!

13
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,590
Whoa-ho-ho! Ho-ho!

14
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:07,890
I'm sorry, fishlegs, did you want that?

15
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:11,630
Oh, snotlout, that was mine!

16
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:13,230
Here you go, babe.

17
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:15,130
Did I tell you that you look amazing today?

18
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:16,260
'Cause you do. Ugh!

19
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:17,530
Come on, barf.

20
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:19,270
It's starting to stink around here.

21
00:02:19,270 --> 00:02:20,530
Nope, still hates you.

22
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,270
Let's blow this place, belch!

23
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:23,540
Aah!

24
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:25,470
All right!

25
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:27,210
Come on!

26
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,380
Oh, yeah!

27
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:33,750
Ah, ha-ha!

28
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:35,820
That's nine for the twins!

29
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:38,150
Astrid lags with three!

30
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:41,820
Fishlegs and snotlout trail with none!

31
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,690
And hiccup is...

32
00:02:43,690 --> 00:02:45,660
Nowhere to be found.

33
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:47,490
Hmm.

34
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,200
Scared him off with the big talk, didn't you, stoick?

35
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:53,930
What are you doing, snotlout?

36
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,640
They're gonna win now.

37
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,310
She's my princess-- whatever she wants, she gets.

38
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:01,210
Ruffnut? Didn't she try to bury you alive?

39
00:03:01,210 --> 00:03:03,580
Only for a few hours.

40
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:05,180
Look at 'em go!

41
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:06,550
Now, dragons used to be

42
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:08,180
a bit of a problem here,

43
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:10,180
but that was five years ago.

44
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,320
Now they've all moved in.

45
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:14,690
And, really, why wouldn't they?

46
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:16,790
We have custom stables,

47
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:18,790
all-you-can-eat feeding stations,

48
00:03:18,790 --> 00:03:21,930
a full-service dragon wash...

49
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:23,960
Even top-of-the-line fire prevention,

50
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:26,400
if I do say so myself.

51
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,440
Ah, it's time, gobber.

52
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:31,240
Righty-ho. Last lap!

53
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:37,840
The black sheep! Come on, stormfly!

54
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:40,780
We can still win this thing!

55
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:43,520
Come on, barf! Let's go!

56
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,520
Go, meatlug!

57
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:49,390
Let's go, let's go! Ha-ha!

58
00:03:49,390 --> 00:03:51,760
This is your big moment.

59
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,930
Have a nice flight.

60
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:58,970
Up! Up, up, up, up, up!

61
00:04:03,010 --> 00:04:05,540
Good job, meatlug!

62
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:07,940
Here you go, darling. Mine's worth ten.

63
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,940
Yeah! The black sheep!

64
00:04:11,310 --> 00:04:13,810
You guys are fighting for ruffnut?

65
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:16,250
I'm totally winning! We're winning together.

66
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:19,320
Oh, no!

67
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,790
- Whoo! No one can stop me now! - Except for me.

68
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:25,460
We're attached, genius.

69
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:26,990
Quit trying to steal hey!

70
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,560
All my glory!

71
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:31,500
- Get them, Astrid! - It's my glory!

72
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,000
- Always ruining everything! - No, sheep, no glory!

73
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,640
Gotcha! Ha-ha!

74
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,040
Whoa! Astrid!

75
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,510
Well played!

76
00:04:40,710 --> 00:04:43,480
That's my future daughter-in-law!

77
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:45,710
Whoo-hoo!

78
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:48,480
Uh, excuse me.

79
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,720
Stormfly!

80
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:55,360
Whoa!

81
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:58,490
Aah!

82
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:03,030
That's 13!

83
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:05,070
Astrid takes the game!

84
00:05:07,370 --> 00:05:09,500
Yep, berk is pretty much perfect.

85
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:11,910
All of my hard work has paid off.

86
00:05:11,910 --> 00:05:13,740
And it's a good thing, too,

87
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,440
because with vikings on the backs of dragons...

88
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:20,580
...the world just got a whole lot bigger.

89
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:37,760
Yeah!

90
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,640
so, what do you think, bud?

91
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:23,680
You want to give this another shot?

92
00:06:24,850 --> 00:06:26,810
Toothless! It'll be fine.

93
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:33,050
Ready?

94
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:36,390
Aah...!

95
00:06:38,130 --> 00:06:40,490
Yeah...!

96
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,700
Whoo-hoo!

97
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:45,830
yeah!

98
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,880
whoa!

99
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:11,160
Oh...

100
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:16,630
Whoo-hoo!

101
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:18,530
Whoa!

102
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,770
Yeah!

103
00:07:21,770 --> 00:07:23,700
Whoo!

104
00:07:24,810 --> 00:07:27,040
This is amazing!

105
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:29,040
No longer amazing.

106
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,080
Toothless!

107
00:07:32,810 --> 00:07:34,080
Oh, no!

108
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:36,750
Oh! Aah!

109
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,020
Aah! Whoa!

110
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:53,130
Whoo!

111
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:55,600
That really came out of nowhere.

112
00:08:02,010 --> 00:08:05,510
We-we got to work on your solo gliding there, bud.

113
00:08:05,510 --> 00:08:07,550
That, uh, locked-up tail

114
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:10,750
makes for some pretty sloppy rescue maneuvers, hey?

115
00:08:26,930 --> 00:08:28,770
ah!

116
00:08:28,770 --> 00:08:31,140
Looks like we found another one, bud.

117
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,610
Oh...!

118
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:37,180
Oh, what, do you want an apology?

119
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,880
Is that why you're pouting,

120
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,080
big baby boo?

121
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:43,920
Well, try this on!

122
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:47,620
Oh, you feeling it yet? Huh?

123
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,060
Picking up on all my heartfelt remorse?

124
00:08:51,590 --> 00:08:54,590
Ah. Yeah. Oh, come on, come on,

125
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,960
you-you wouldn't hurt a one-legged...

126
00:08:56,970 --> 00:08:58,270
Uh...

127
00:08:58,270 --> 00:08:59,800
Y-you're right, you're right.

128
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,300
You win. You win.

129
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,000
Whoa-whoa-whoa...

130
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:04,140
He's down!

131
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:06,140
And it's ugly!

132
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,740
Dragons and vikings...

133
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:09,140
Enemies again...

134
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:11,580
Locked in combat to the bitter...

135
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:13,550
Oh...!

136
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:21,020
You know that doesn't wash out.

137
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:48,180
so, what should we name it?

138
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:50,820
"Itchy armpit" It is.

139
00:09:51,890 --> 00:09:53,320
What do you reckon, bud?

140
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:56,190
Think we might find a few timberjacks in those woods?

141
00:09:56,190 --> 00:09:59,290
The odd whispering death or two in the rocks?

142
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:03,930
Who knows, maybe we'll finally track down

143
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:05,700
another night fury.

144
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,870
Wouldn't that be something.

145
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:10,900
So, what do you say?

146
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:12,340
Just keep going?

147
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:24,080
Afternoon, milady.

148
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:28,090
Where have you been? Hi.

149
00:10:28,090 --> 00:10:31,360
Oh, winning races. What else?

150
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,690
The real question is,

151
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,000
where have you been?

152
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,030
- Avoiding my dad. - Oh, no. What happened now?

153
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:40,370
Oh, you're gonna... You're gonna love this.

154
00:10:40,370 --> 00:10:42,400
I wake up, the sun's shining,

155
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,040
terrible terrors are

156
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,210
singing on the rooftop,

157
00:10:45,210 --> 00:10:46,870
I saunter down to breakfast

158
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,280
thinking all is right with the world, and I get:

159
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:51,850
"Son, we need to talk."

160
00:10:51,850 --> 00:10:54,710
"Not, now, dad. I got a whole day of goofing off

161
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:55,880
to get started."

162
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,650
Okay, first of all,

163
00:10:57,650 --> 00:11:00,250
I-I don't sound like that. What is this character?

164
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:02,260
And-and second...

165
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:04,690
What is that thing you're doing with my shoulders?

166
00:11:04,690 --> 00:11:08,030
Yeah, that's-that's a really flattering impersonation.

167
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:10,000
Anyway, he goes...

168
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,170
"You're the pride of berk, son,

169
00:11:12,170 --> 00:11:15,440
and I couldn't be prouder." Aw, thanks, dad.

170
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:18,270
I'm pretty impressed with myself, too.

171
00:11:18,270 --> 00:11:21,240
When have I ever done that with my hands?

172
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,880
You just did!

173
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,810
Okay, just...

174
00:11:24,810 --> 00:11:26,210
Hold... still.

175
00:11:27,450 --> 00:11:29,850
Very serious. Mm-hmm.

176
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,420
"You're all grown up,

177
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:36,260
"And since no chief could ask for a better successor,

178
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:38,930
- I've decided..." - To make you chief! Oh, my gods!

179
00:11:38,930 --> 00:11:41,090
Hiccup, that's amazing!

180
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,700
Oh...!

181
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:45,000
Y-you're gonna wear out the spring coil.

182
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,300
The calibration is very sensitive.

183
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:54,910
Yeah, so... this is

184
00:11:54,910 --> 00:11:56,780
what I'm dealing with.

185
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:58,040
What did you tell him?

186
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,410
I-I didn't.

187
00:11:59,410 --> 00:12:00,810
By the time he turned around, I was gone.

188
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,180
Huh.

189
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:05,990
Well... it's a lot of responsibility.

190
00:12:05,990 --> 00:12:08,290
The map will have to wait, for sure,

191
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:09,920
and... and I'll need

192
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:12,830
to fly toothless, since you'll be too busy, but...

193
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:18,330
I-it's not me, Astrid.

194
00:12:18,330 --> 00:12:21,500
All those speeches and planning and running the village,

195
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,140
that's his thing.

196
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:25,340
I think you're missing the point.

197
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:26,940
I mean-- chief.

198
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:28,370
What an honor!

199
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:29,940
I'd be pretty excited.

200
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:32,850
I-I... I'm not like you.

201
00:12:32,850 --> 00:12:35,120
You... know exactly who you are,

202
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:37,450
you always have, but...

203
00:12:37,450 --> 00:12:39,490
I'm still looking.

204
00:12:39,490 --> 00:12:42,260
I know that I'm not my father,

205
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:45,290
and I never met my mother, so...

206
00:12:45,290 --> 00:12:47,430
What does that make me?

207
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:57,370
What you're searching for isn't out there, hiccup...

208
00:12:57,370 --> 00:12:59,940
It's in here.

209
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:03,080
Maybe you just don't see it yet.

210
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:05,110
Ugh. Ugh! Maybe.

211
00:13:05,110 --> 00:13:06,910
But, you know...

212
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,780
There is something out there.

213
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:11,480
Hiccup...

214
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,450
Wow...

215
00:13:45,990 --> 00:13:48,590
Stay close.

216
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:02,570
What happened here?

217
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:10,080
All right, e-easy, bud.

218
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:11,440
Hiccup!

219
00:14:11,450 --> 00:14:14,110
Fire! Astrid, look out!

220
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,090
Aah! Hiccup!

221
00:14:23,930 --> 00:14:25,390
Watch the tail!

222
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:29,030
Tie those legs up!

223
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,370
Huh?

224
00:14:32,370 --> 00:14:35,440
Is that what I think it is? Hiccup: Stop!

225
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,170
Stormfly!

226
00:14:37,170 --> 00:14:38,610
What are you doing?!

227
00:14:38,610 --> 00:14:40,270
Ooh!

228
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,440
Back again!

229
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:46,380
Soil my britches.

230
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:49,180
That is a night fury.

231
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,280
Thought they were all gone for good.

232
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:53,020
Looks like our luck's had a turn

233
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:54,390
for the better, lads!

234
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:56,360
Don't think drago has one of those...

235
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,190
In his dragon army.

236
00:14:58,190 --> 00:14:59,490
Dragon army?

237
00:14:59,490 --> 00:15:01,490
Look, we don't want any trouble.

238
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,930
Hah! You should have thought of that

239
00:15:03,930 --> 00:15:06,400
before you stole all of our dragons

240
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,970
and blasted our fort to bits!

241
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:09,670
That's right! Man 2: Yeah, look it at!

242
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:11,100
Wait.

243
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:12,340
What are you talking about?

244
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:13,970
You think we did this?

245
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:17,580
Hah! Dragon trapping is hard enough work as it is

246
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:20,010
without do-gooder dragon riders

247
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:23,980
sneaking in to rescue them. What do-gooder...?

248
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:26,650
There are other dragon riders? You mean

249
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:29,560
other than your thieving friend from last night? You tell me.

250
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,020
You may have

251
00:15:31,030 --> 00:15:32,660
an ice-spitting dragon on your side,

252
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:35,230
but we still have a quota to fill.

253
00:15:35,230 --> 00:15:37,460
How do you suppose we explain this mess

254
00:15:37,470 --> 00:15:39,000
to drago bludvist?

255
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,500
Drago what-fist?

256
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,500
Does anything you say make sense?

257
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,340
He's expecting a new shipment of dragons

258
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:46,540
for his army by tomorrow.

259
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:50,240
And drago don't take well to excuses!

260
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:52,080
This is what he gave me

261
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:54,450
last time I showed up empty-handed.

262
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:58,550
He promised to be far less understanding in the future.

263
00:15:58,550 --> 00:16:01,420
All right, look, we don't know anything about a dragon thief

264
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,690
or an ice-spitting dragon

265
00:16:02,690 --> 00:16:04,690
or your lunatic boss

266
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:07,130
and his dragon army, okay?

267
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:10,230
Just give us back our dragon, and we'll go...

268
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:13,030
Strange, hostile person whom we've never met.

269
00:16:13,030 --> 00:16:15,030
Oh, where are my manners?

270
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,440
I'm eret...

271
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:19,240
Son of eret.

272
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,510
Finest dragon trapper alive.

273
00:16:21,510 --> 00:16:23,310
Yeah. After all...

274
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:27,280
It's not just anyone who can capture a night fury.

275
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,320
And this is toothless.

276
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,580
He says we're going. Now.

277
00:16:31,590 --> 00:16:32,720
Hah!

278
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,320
They all say that.

279
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,590
Rush 'em, lads!

280
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:44,060
Stormfly, come on!

281
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:45,330
Go! Go!

282
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,340
You will

283
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,210
never hold on to those dragons!

284
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:53,510
You hear me?!

285
00:16:53,510 --> 00:16:56,280
Drago is coming for them all!

286
00:16:58,780 --> 00:17:02,550
Come on, meatlug! Whoo-hoo! Yahoo!

287
00:17:11,190 --> 00:17:12,290
Hey there, stoick! Hey, how are you?

288
00:17:12,290 --> 00:17:13,760
Beautiful day.

289
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:16,060
Hello, spitelout. Great race. Yeah...

290
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,630
Oh! Sorry, Mrs. Ack.

291
00:17:17,630 --> 00:17:20,330
Any sign of him? Eh! He's probably flown

292
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:22,640
off the edge of the world by now.

293
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:25,100
You sure you want that kid running the village?

294
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:27,210
You can still delay your retirement.

295
00:17:27,210 --> 00:17:29,780
Oh, he's ready. You'll see.

296
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:32,380
There he is!

297
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:35,050
Huh? The pride of berk!

298
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:39,650
Who finally decided to show up for work. Yay.

299
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:41,420
Sorry, got held up. Hey, uh, dad,

300
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,760
could I have a word?

301
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:44,420
Something you're itching to tell me?

302
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:47,460
Uh, not quite the itch you're thinking of, but, yes.

303
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:48,660
Oh, good man!

304
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:50,700
Now, lesson one: A chief's first duty

305
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,070
is to his people,

306
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:53,400
so... 41!

307
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:55,270
Well, can we just talk in private for...

308
00:17:55,270 --> 00:17:56,300
Forty... Man: That's me!

309
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:57,540
That's me! I'm next!

310
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:58,600
Hey, I was ahead of you!

311
00:17:58,610 --> 00:18:00,110
If we could just talk...

312
00:18:00,110 --> 00:18:02,180
Excuse me. I've been here all day.

313
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:04,540
Okay, okay, I want one of those high seaters

314
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:07,810
with lots of spikes and a big storage compartment!

315
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:11,320
Absolutely! You got it, sir. Dad, this is actually

316
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:13,120
a little more important than building saddles.

317
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:15,290
Ah, lesson two: No task is too small

318
00:18:15,290 --> 00:18:17,190
when it comes to serving your people.

319
00:18:17,190 --> 00:18:19,290
But, dad... Oh, excuse us, grump.

320
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:21,590
Can we just talk... Yah! Grump!

321
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,830
You let the forge die down again!

322
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:29,670
Ah...

323
00:18:29,670 --> 00:18:31,700
That's it, grump! You're going up for adoption.

324
00:18:31,710 --> 00:18:33,310
Okay, uh... There you go.

325
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:35,580
Dad... yeah, but seriously, go on. Have away.

326
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:40,110
I really need to tell you about this new land we came across.

327
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:41,780
Another one? Any new dragons?

328
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:43,650
We didn't stick around to find out.

329
00:18:43,650 --> 00:18:46,420
These folks weren't particularly friendly.

330
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,590
Oh, really?

331
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:49,360
Your night fury and deadly nadder

332
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,820
didn't bring them cheering to the rooftops?

333
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:53,360
No, this was different.

334
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:55,330
Not the standard run-for-the-hills hoo-ha

335
00:18:55,330 --> 00:18:56,660
I've come to enjoy.

336
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:59,600
These guys were trappers.

337
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,370
Dragon trappers.

338
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:02,800
You should have seen their fort.

339
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:05,810
All blown apart and stuck in giant spikes of ice.

340
00:19:05,810 --> 00:19:07,270
It was weird.

341
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:08,880
I've never seen anything like it.

342
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:11,540
A-and worst of all, they thought we did it!

343
00:19:11,550 --> 00:19:14,380
You know, you two are gonna get yourselves in serious trouble

344
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,720
one of these days.

345
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:18,890
Not everyone appreciates this way of life.

346
00:19:18,890 --> 00:19:20,190
Aye, gobber's right, son.

347
00:19:20,190 --> 00:19:21,850
Best we keep to our own.

348
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:24,920
Besides, you'll have more important uses for your time.

349
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:26,760
Huh-huh?

350
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,660
Once we make the big announcement!

351
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:32,670
They are building a dragon army.

352
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:37,700
Or-or at least the guy they work for is. Uh...

353
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:40,540
"Dargo... bloody fist" Or something.

354
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,540
I'll bloody his fist with my face

355
00:19:44,550 --> 00:19:46,610
if he tries to take my dragon!

356
00:19:46,610 --> 00:19:47,650
Or mine!

357
00:19:47,650 --> 00:19:49,380
Ugh! You're such a moron.

358
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:50,650
A beautiful moron.

359
00:19:50,650 --> 00:19:52,190
Yeah.

360
00:19:52,190 --> 00:19:55,350
Bludvist? Drago bludvist?

361
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,190
Uh, yeah. Wait...

362
00:19:57,190 --> 00:19:58,720
You know him?

363
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:03,800
Ground all dragons! Hiccup: What? Why?

364
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:05,670
Seal the gates!

365
00:20:05,670 --> 00:20:07,800
Lower the storm doors! Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait, wait.

366
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:09,370
What is happening? Gobber: Come on!

367
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:10,740
You heard the man! Lock it down!

368
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:14,440
Stoick: No dragon or viking

369
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,640
sets foot off this island until I give the word!

370
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,750
Wait, because some guy you knew is stirring up trouble

371
00:20:19,750 --> 00:20:20,980
in some faraway land?

372
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:23,920
Because drago bludvist is a madman

373
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,350
without conscience or mercy.

374
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:28,250
And if he's built a dragon army,

375
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,820
gods help us all.

376
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:30,990
Get them into their pens!

377
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:32,730
Quickly! Aye, stoick.

378
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:34,660
Then let's ride back out there.

379
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:36,660
We'll follow those trappers to drago

380
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:38,460
and talk some sense into him.

381
00:20:38,470 --> 00:20:39,930
No. We fortify the island.

382
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:41,970
It's our duty to keep the peace.

383
00:20:41,970 --> 00:20:43,700
Peace is over, hiccup.

384
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:46,710
- I must prepare you for war. - War?

385
00:20:46,710 --> 00:20:48,980
Dad, if drago's coming for our dragons,

386
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:51,840
we can't wait around for him to get here.

387
00:20:51,850 --> 00:20:55,310
Let's go find him and change his mind.

388
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,320
No, some minds won't be changed, hiccup.

389
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:59,720
Berk is what you need to worry about.

390
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:02,290
A chief protects his own.

391
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:06,260
Secure the stables! Latch every stall!

392
00:21:06,260 --> 00:21:08,260
- Hiccup, don't. - I have to.

393
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:09,600
This way!

394
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,800
Quickly!

395
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Hiccup!

396
00:21:15,670 --> 00:21:16,840
Come on!

397
00:21:18,270 --> 00:21:20,310
Hiccup! Aah!

398
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:32,350
Keep your eyes peeled, lads!

399
00:21:32,350 --> 00:21:35,390
With this wind, we'll reach drago by daybreak.

400
00:21:35,390 --> 00:21:38,760
So best we fill this ship up with dragons, and quick!

401
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:40,360
It's no time to be picky!

402
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,630
Uh, eret?

403
00:21:41,630 --> 00:21:43,860
Not if we want to keep our...

404
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:46,630
...heads!

405
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:48,570
Off the port quarter!

406
00:21:48,570 --> 00:21:50,770
Net them, lads! Take them down!

407
00:21:50,770 --> 00:21:53,310
There's two of them! Up on the left!

408
00:21:53,310 --> 00:21:56,410
You're not getting away this time.

409
00:21:56,410 --> 00:21:57,580
Fire!

410
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,580
Reload! Reload!

411
00:21:59,580 --> 00:22:02,750
Come on, reload! Incoming!

412
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:03,980
Steady yourselves, mates.

413
00:22:03,990 --> 00:22:06,350
And here I was,

414
00:22:06,350 --> 00:22:08,650
worried we might turn up empty-handed.

415
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,690
Nope. It's your lucky day.

416
00:22:10,690 --> 00:22:12,020
We give up.

417
00:22:13,430 --> 00:22:15,090
That's one night fury,

418
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,800
uh, one deadly nadder, and...

419
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:20,830
Two of the finest dragon riders west of luk tuk.

420
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:22,640
That ought to make the boss happy, right?

421
00:22:23,810 --> 00:22:25,400
Excuse us.

422
00:22:25,410 --> 00:22:26,640
: What are you doing?

423
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,340
Toothless, stay.

424
00:22:29,710 --> 00:22:31,680
Uh, the dragons don't really care

425
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:34,080
for cramped spaces, so they'll just hang out with you.

426
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,680
They won't be any trouble.

427
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:39,020
Unless you do that.

428
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:41,490
You know, wooden boats, big ocean...

429
00:22:41,490 --> 00:22:43,360
H-how is your swimming?

430
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:44,790
Not good.

431
00:22:45,830 --> 00:22:47,790
Oops. Almost forget.

432
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:50,100
- Can't have armed prisoners. - Give me that.

433
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:51,830
How is this a plan?

434
00:22:51,830 --> 00:22:54,770
Just what every dragon trapper needs.

435
00:22:54,770 --> 00:22:58,100
One end coats the blade in monstrous nightmare saliva.

436
00:22:58,110 --> 00:23:00,870
The other sprays hideous zippleback gas.

437
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,740
All it takes is a spark, and...

438
00:23:04,810 --> 00:23:06,410
Oh, yeah, there you go.

439
00:23:07,850 --> 00:23:09,850
Once they see you as one of their own,

440
00:23:09,850 --> 00:23:11,080
even the testiest dragons can be trained.

441
00:23:11,090 --> 00:23:12,420
Right, bud?

442
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:15,450
Give me that!

443
00:23:15,460 --> 00:23:17,460
What game are you playing?

444
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:19,730
Uh, no game. We just want to meet drago.

445
00:23:19,730 --> 00:23:21,460
Why?

446
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:23,930
Because I'm going to change his mind about dragons.

447
00:23:27,470 --> 00:23:29,800
He can be really persuasive.

448
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:31,470
Once you've earned his loyalty,

449
00:23:31,470 --> 00:23:34,010
there is nothing a dragon won't do for you.

450
00:23:34,010 --> 00:23:37,480
You won't be changing any minds around here.

451
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:40,880
I can change yours, right here, right now.

452
00:23:43,050 --> 00:23:44,720
uh, may I?

453
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:45,850
Waah!

454
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:50,720
Watch it! Eret: Dragon riders!

455
00:23:58,130 --> 00:23:59,530
Put me down!

456
00:23:59,530 --> 00:24:01,600
Snotlout, what-what are you doing?

457
00:24:01,600 --> 00:24:03,540
See how well I protect and provide?

458
00:24:04,740 --> 00:24:05,870
What is with all the nets?

459
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:07,710
Hey, watch it! That was...

460
00:24:07,710 --> 00:24:10,010
Close.

461
00:24:12,810 --> 00:24:15,110
Oh, my.

462
00:24:18,750 --> 00:24:20,090
Me likey.

463
00:24:23,590 --> 00:24:25,990
Take me.

464
00:24:29,030 --> 00:24:30,230
Hold your fire!

465
00:24:35,070 --> 00:24:37,000
Um, what are you guys doing here?

466
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,170
We're here to rescue you!

467
00:24:39,170 --> 00:24:40,940
I don't need to be rescued.

468
00:24:40,940 --> 00:24:42,780
Enough!

469
00:24:43,810 --> 00:24:46,180
Well, didn't you just pick

470
00:24:46,180 --> 00:24:47,980
the wrong ship, eh?

471
00:24:47,980 --> 00:24:49,820
I am eret, son of...

472
00:24:49,820 --> 00:24:50,820
Eret...

473
00:24:52,250 --> 00:24:53,620
I...

474
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:57,160
Get this thing off me.

475
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,820
Anyone else?

476
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:00,690
Hmm, that's what I figured.

477
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:02,800
You, saddle up.

478
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,000
We're going home.

479
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,030
No.

480
00:25:06,030 --> 00:25:07,930
Of all the irresponsible...

481
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:10,900
I'm trying to protect our dragons and stop a war.

482
00:25:10,910 --> 00:25:12,140
How is that irresponsible?

483
00:25:12,140 --> 00:25:14,770
Because war is what he wants, son!

484
00:25:20,750 --> 00:25:23,720
Years ago, there was a great gathering of chieftains

485
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:26,250
to discuss the dragon scourge we all faced.

486
00:25:26,250 --> 00:25:30,790
Into our midst came a stranger from a strange land,

487
00:25:30,790 --> 00:25:34,560
covered in scars and draped in a cloak of dragon skin.

488
00:25:35,630 --> 00:25:37,230
He carried no weapon

489
00:25:37,230 --> 00:25:38,930
and spoke softly,

490
00:25:38,930 --> 00:25:40,270
saying that he,

491
00:25:40,270 --> 00:25:42,640
drago bludvist,

492
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:44,700
was a man of the people,

493
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:49,280
devoted to freeing mankind from the tyranny of dragons.

494
00:25:49,280 --> 00:25:51,740
He claimed that he alone could control the dragons,

495
00:25:51,750 --> 00:25:54,110
and that he alone could keep us safe,

496
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:57,250
if we chose to bow down

497
00:25:57,250 --> 00:26:00,790
and follow him.

498
00:26:02,260 --> 00:26:04,620
Stupid. Ah, good one.

499
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:06,830
Aye, we laughed, too...

500
00:26:06,830 --> 00:26:08,130
Until he wrapped himself in his cloak

501
00:26:08,130 --> 00:26:09,760
and cried out,

502
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:11,630
"Then see how well you do without me!"

503
00:26:11,630 --> 00:26:13,170
...See how well you do without me!

504
00:26:13,170 --> 00:26:16,200
The rooftop suddenly burst into flames,

505
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:20,010
and from it, armored dragons descended,

506
00:26:20,010 --> 00:26:23,140
burning the hall to the ground.

507
00:26:23,140 --> 00:26:25,980
I...

508
00:26:25,980 --> 00:26:28,610
Was the only one to escape.

509
00:26:33,250 --> 00:26:37,190
Men who kill without reason cannot be reasoned with.

510
00:26:37,190 --> 00:26:39,060
- Maybe. - Hiccup!

511
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:41,130
I'm still going to try.

512
00:26:42,930 --> 00:26:44,800
This is what I'm good at,

513
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:46,800
and-and if I could change your mind,

514
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:49,270
I can change his, too.

515
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:52,300
Come on.

516
00:26:53,340 --> 00:26:54,670
- Let's go. - No!

517
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,610
Lead the others back to berk.

518
00:26:56,610 --> 00:26:59,040
I've had enough mutiny for one day.

519
00:27:01,350 --> 00:27:03,120
Ooh, I like that.

520
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:04,880
Stoick: Ruffnut!

521
00:27:04,890 --> 00:27:06,720
Okay!

522
00:27:07,750 --> 00:27:09,720
Ah.

523
00:27:27,310 --> 00:27:28,970
Don't worry, bud.

524
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:31,940
I'm not gonna let anything happen to you.

525
00:27:31,950 --> 00:27:34,650
I promise.

526
00:27:42,190 --> 00:27:43,960
Aw, come on, dad.

527
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:45,660
Really?

528
00:27:53,670 --> 00:27:55,400
Okay.

529
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,400
No sudden moves.

530
00:28:21,730 --> 00:28:23,130
hold on, hold on.

531
00:28:34,940 --> 00:28:37,410
Toothless...!

532
00:29:25,490 --> 00:29:27,090
hey!

533
00:29:27,090 --> 00:29:28,860
You left my dragon back there!

534
00:29:28,860 --> 00:29:31,300
He can't fly on his own! He'll drown!

535
00:29:53,450 --> 00:29:55,790
Hey! Uh...

536
00:29:55,790 --> 00:29:57,820
We have to head back for my dragon!

537
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:46,000
Who are you?

538
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:48,870
The dragon thief?

539
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:50,310
Uh...

540
00:30:50,310 --> 00:30:52,580
Drago bludvist?

541
00:30:52,580 --> 00:30:54,480
Do you even understand

542
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,480
what I'm saying?

543
00:31:01,490 --> 00:31:03,220
Toothless!

544
00:31:03,220 --> 00:31:06,020
Oh, it's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

545
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:08,130
I'm glad to see you, too, bud.

546
00:31:08,130 --> 00:31:09,360
You really had me worried there.

547
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:48,530
Uh, uh...

548
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:56,170
Oh...

549
00:31:56,180 --> 00:31:57,480
Hiccup?

550
00:31:57,480 --> 00:31:59,380
Uh...

551
00:32:01,980 --> 00:32:03,650
C-could it be?

552
00:32:03,650 --> 00:32:06,990
After all these years?

553
00:32:06,990 --> 00:32:09,490
How is this possible?

554
00:32:09,490 --> 00:32:12,120
Uh, should I...

555
00:32:12,130 --> 00:32:13,460
Should I know you?

556
00:32:13,460 --> 00:32:15,630
No.

557
00:32:15,630 --> 00:32:17,330
You were only a babe.

558
00:32:23,040 --> 00:32:25,440
But a mother never forgets.

559
00:32:29,180 --> 00:32:31,140
Shh, shh.

560
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:35,350
Come.

561
00:32:35,350 --> 00:32:37,180
Boar-headed!

562
00:32:37,180 --> 00:32:38,520
Just like his mother!

563
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:40,520
Aye, she could never stay put, either.

564
00:32:40,520 --> 00:32:41,590
Eh, he's just 20,

565
00:32:41,590 --> 00:32:43,160
and a viking.

566
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:44,620
I mean, could there be a worse combination?

567
00:32:44,630 --> 00:32:48,130
Heh! When I think of how stubborn and senseless

568
00:32:48,130 --> 00:32:50,560
you were back in the day.

569
00:32:50,560 --> 00:32:52,260
Oh.

570
00:32:52,270 --> 00:32:55,000
Well, not much has changed, actually.

571
00:32:56,600 --> 00:32:58,240
Ah, you know what he's like.

572
00:32:58,240 --> 00:33:00,110
He won't give up, gobber.

573
00:33:00,110 --> 00:33:02,710
And if hiccup finds drago

574
00:33:02,710 --> 00:33:05,040
before we find him...

575
00:33:05,050 --> 00:33:06,580
Ah! Nothing can hurt hiccup,

576
00:33:06,580 --> 00:33:08,710
so long as that night fury's around.

577
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,180
It's a night fury!

578
00:33:13,550 --> 00:33:16,250
Huh?

579
00:33:29,740 --> 00:33:31,440
Find them, skullcrusher.

580
00:33:33,140 --> 00:33:34,470
Find them.

581
00:33:41,750 --> 00:33:43,680
Uh, h-hold on. Wait just a minute.

582
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:45,080
- This way. - Come back here.

583
00:33:45,090 --> 00:33:46,720
- Come. - You can't just say

584
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:49,020
something like that and run off.

585
00:33:49,020 --> 00:33:50,490
You're my mother?!

586
00:33:50,490 --> 00:33:52,090
I mean, what the...?

587
00:33:52,090 --> 00:33:54,130
Do you... do you grasp how insane it sounds?

588
00:33:54,130 --> 00:33:55,360
Come quickly.

589
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:56,530
I have questions!

590
00:33:56,530 --> 00:33:58,400
Where have you...

591
00:33:58,400 --> 00:34:00,400
Been all this time?

592
00:34:01,570 --> 00:34:03,400
What-what have you been doing?

593
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:06,340
But they-they said you were dead!

594
00:34:06,340 --> 00:34:08,670
Everyone thinks you were eaten by...

595
00:34:49,150 --> 00:34:52,780
This is where you've been for 20 years?

596
00:34:54,590 --> 00:34:57,790
You-you've been rescuing them.

597
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:02,630
Unbelievable.

598
00:35:02,630 --> 00:35:04,360
- You're not upset? - What?

599
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:06,160
No. I-I don't know. I...

600
00:35:06,170 --> 00:35:08,830
It's a bit much to get my head around, to be Frank.

601
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:11,700
It's not every day you find out your mother

602
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:15,870
is some kind of crazy, feral, vigilante dragon lady.

603
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:18,280
Oh...

604
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:19,880
Well...

605
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:23,450
At least I'm not boring, right?

606
00:35:23,450 --> 00:35:25,220
Well, I suppose there is that...

607
00:35:25,220 --> 00:35:28,320
One specific thing.

608
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:30,160
Do-do you like it?

609
00:35:30,160 --> 00:35:31,220
I...

610
00:35:31,230 --> 00:35:32,490
I... i...

611
00:35:32,490 --> 00:35:34,460
I-I don't have the words.

612
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:44,600
C-can I...

613
00:35:44,610 --> 00:35:46,870
Oh, he's beautiful.

614
00:35:46,870 --> 00:35:48,470
Oh.

615
00:35:50,140 --> 00:35:51,310
Oh, incredible.

616
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:55,880
He might very well be the last of his kind.

617
00:35:55,880 --> 00:35:58,350
Oh... and look,

618
00:35:58,350 --> 00:35:59,890
he's your age.

619
00:35:59,890 --> 00:36:01,290
Wow.

620
00:36:01,290 --> 00:36:03,160
No wonder you get along so well.

621
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:04,490
Oh, yeah? Oh, yeah?

622
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:08,890
And retractable teeth.

623
00:36:08,900 --> 00:36:11,200
How did you manage...

624
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:12,730
I found him in the woods.

625
00:36:12,730 --> 00:36:16,300
He was shot down and wounded.

626
00:36:19,940 --> 00:36:22,670
This snafflefang lost his leg

627
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:25,380
to one of drago bludvist's iron traps.

628
00:36:25,380 --> 00:36:26,850
This raincutter

629
00:36:26,850 --> 00:36:29,210
had her wing sliced by razor netting.

630
00:36:29,220 --> 00:36:31,580
And this, oh, poor hobblegrunt

631
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:34,490
was blinded by a tree snare

632
00:36:34,490 --> 00:36:37,720
and then left to die alone and scared.

633
00:36:37,720 --> 00:36:39,790
And what of this?

634
00:36:39,790 --> 00:36:42,790
Did drago or his trappers do this, too?

635
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:44,330
Oh.

636
00:36:44,330 --> 00:36:45,830
Yeah.

637
00:36:45,830 --> 00:36:49,570
Well, crazy thing is...

638
00:36:49,570 --> 00:36:53,510
I'm actually the one who shot him down.

639
00:36:53,510 --> 00:36:56,270
Hey, it's-it's okay, though.

640
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:57,340
He got me back.

641
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:58,740
Right, bud?

642
00:36:58,750 --> 00:37:00,710
You couldn't save all of me, could you?

643
00:37:00,710 --> 00:37:02,480
You just had to make it even.

644
00:37:02,480 --> 00:37:05,350
So peg leg.

645
00:37:08,850 --> 00:37:10,460
Uh...

646
00:37:10,460 --> 00:37:12,960
What did your father think of your night fury friend?

647
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:15,990
Oh, he-he didn't take it all that well.

648
00:37:17,300 --> 00:37:19,860
But then, he changed.

649
00:37:19,870 --> 00:37:21,000
They all did.

650
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:22,600
Pretty soon,

651
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:25,440
everyone back home had dragons of their own.

652
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:27,640
If only it were possible.

653
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:28,740
No, really.

654
00:37:28,740 --> 00:37:30,810
Believe me, I tried, as well,

655
00:37:30,810 --> 00:37:33,850
but people are not capable of change, hiccup.

656
00:37:33,850 --> 00:37:35,380
Some of us...

657
00:37:35,380 --> 00:37:37,650
Were just born different.

658
00:37:43,920 --> 00:37:46,860
Berk was a land of kill

659
00:37:46,860 --> 00:37:48,430
or be killed,

660
00:37:48,430 --> 00:37:51,400
but I believed peace was possible.

661
00:37:52,670 --> 00:37:55,670
Stop! You'll only make it worse!

662
00:37:55,670 --> 00:37:59,340
It was a very unpopular opinion.

663
00:38:00,610 --> 00:38:02,510
Hiccup!

664
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:04,310
Then one night,

665
00:38:04,310 --> 00:38:07,410
a dragon broke into our house, finding you

666
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:08,980
in the cradle.

667
00:38:08,980 --> 00:38:12,350
I rushed to protect you.

668
00:38:16,020 --> 00:38:21,330
But what I saw was proof of everything I believed.

669
00:38:34,040 --> 00:38:36,740
This wasn't a vicious beast,

670
00:38:36,740 --> 00:38:39,680
but an intelligent, gentle creature,

671
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:43,380
whose soul reflected my own.

672
00:38:45,020 --> 00:38:48,390
- Valka, run! - No, don't.

673
00:38:50,590 --> 00:38:52,890
Oh...

674
00:38:52,890 --> 00:38:54,060
Hold on!

675
00:38:55,760 --> 00:38:58,100
No! Aah! Stoick!

676
00:38:58,100 --> 00:39:00,470
Valka!

677
00:39:01,430 --> 00:39:04,070
Stoick!

678
00:39:04,070 --> 00:39:06,810
Valka.

679
00:39:06,810 --> 00:39:10,080
You and your father nearly died

680
00:39:10,080 --> 00:39:11,680
that night.

681
00:39:11,680 --> 00:39:14,680
All because I couldn't kill a dragon.

682
00:39:14,680 --> 00:39:17,880
Eh, runs in the family.

683
00:39:17,880 --> 00:39:19,950
It broke my heart to stay away,

684
00:39:19,950 --> 00:39:23,420
but I believed you'd be safer if I did.

685
00:39:24,820 --> 00:39:26,560
How did you survive?

686
00:39:26,560 --> 00:39:28,830
Oh, cloudjumper never meant to harm me.

687
00:39:28,830 --> 00:39:32,960
He must have thought I belonged here

688
00:39:32,970 --> 00:39:36,900
in the home of the great bewilderbeast.

689
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:40,110
The Alpha species.

690
00:39:40,110 --> 00:39:41,970
One of the very few

691
00:39:41,980 --> 00:39:43,940
that still exist.

692
00:39:46,550 --> 00:39:47,680
Every nest has its queen,

693
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:51,120
but this is the king of all dragons.

694
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:53,520
With his icy breath,

695
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:56,120
this graceful giant built our nest,

696
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:59,560
a safe haven for dragons everywhere.

697
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:01,860
Wait, that's the ice-spitter?

698
00:40:01,860 --> 00:40:03,730
He's responsible

699
00:40:03,730 --> 00:40:04,900
for all that destruction?

700
00:40:04,900 --> 00:40:06,770
He protects us.

701
00:40:06,770 --> 00:40:09,100
We all live under his care

702
00:40:09,100 --> 00:40:10,940
and his command.

703
00:40:13,870 --> 00:40:16,010
All but the babies, of course...

704
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:20,610
...who listen to no one.

705
00:40:23,580 --> 00:40:25,550
Aw...

706
00:40:34,460 --> 00:40:36,530
I've lived among them for 20 years, hiccup,

707
00:40:36,530 --> 00:40:39,130
discovering their secrets.

708
00:40:42,070 --> 00:40:44,670
He likes you.

709
00:40:44,670 --> 00:40:46,170
Wow.

710
00:40:46,170 --> 00:40:47,710
You must be hungry.

711
00:40:47,710 --> 00:40:49,470
Uh, yeah, I could eat.

712
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:50,480
Good.

713
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:51,880
It's feeding time.

714
00:41:00,550 --> 00:41:02,620
I don't like it.

715
00:41:02,620 --> 00:41:04,760
They should've been back with hiccup by now.

716
00:41:04,760 --> 00:41:05,920
I don't like it, either.

717
00:41:05,930 --> 00:41:07,030
Eret, son of eret,

718
00:41:07,030 --> 00:41:08,790
was the man of my dreams.

719
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,200
My everything!

720
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:12,660
But, baby, I grew facial hair for you.

721
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:14,600
Me, too.

722
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:16,100
What if drago shot them down?

723
00:41:16,100 --> 00:41:18,800
What if they need our help?

724
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:20,570
We have to find them.

725
00:41:20,570 --> 00:41:21,610
Wait, wait, what?

726
00:41:21,610 --> 00:41:22,770
No, but stoick said...

727
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:24,010
It doesn't matter what he said

728
00:41:24,010 --> 00:41:25,210
if they've all been captured.

729
00:41:25,210 --> 00:41:26,580
Come on!

730
00:41:29,580 --> 00:41:31,680
Do we go back?

731
00:41:31,690 --> 00:41:32,950
We've nowhere to go,

732
00:41:32,950 --> 00:41:34,950
nothing to sell, and no heads

733
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:36,220
to call our own.

734
00:41:36,220 --> 00:41:37,860
- Uh, eret...? - If we don't turn up

735
00:41:37,860 --> 00:41:40,230
with dragons and fast...

736
00:41:41,760 --> 00:41:43,760
Careful what you wish for!

737
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:45,530
Do something! Eret, son of eret!

738
00:41:45,530 --> 00:41:46,530
We'll miss you, eret!

739
00:41:46,530 --> 00:41:47,530
What is this?

740
00:41:47,530 --> 00:41:48,700
A kidnapping.

741
00:41:48,700 --> 00:41:50,240
Yay, can he ride with me? Can he?

742
00:41:50,240 --> 00:41:51,540
Can he...?

743
00:41:52,910 --> 00:41:54,910
You're gonna show us the way to drago.

744
00:41:54,910 --> 00:41:56,570
And help dragon riders

745
00:41:56,580 --> 00:41:58,080
sneak into drago's camp?

746
00:41:58,080 --> 00:41:59,140
Just kill me now.

747
00:41:59,150 --> 00:42:00,250
That could be arranged.

748
00:42:00,250 --> 00:42:01,910
Stormfly, drop it.

749
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:03,580
Huh?

750
00:42:04,580 --> 00:42:05,850
Good girl!

751
00:42:05,850 --> 00:42:08,890
Stormfly, fetch.

752
00:42:09,890 --> 00:42:10,990
All right!

753
00:42:10,990 --> 00:42:13,960
Okay! I'll take you to drago!

754
00:42:15,860 --> 00:42:17,600
Works every time.

755
00:42:25,770 --> 00:42:28,270
Hey, I-I thought we were going to eat.

756
00:42:28,280 --> 00:42:30,040
Oh, we are.

757
00:43:00,840 --> 00:43:04,110
And then, from dragon island, I found this archipelago...

758
00:43:11,050 --> 00:43:12,920
There.

759
00:43:12,920 --> 00:43:15,650
Whoa.

760
00:44:05,140 --> 00:44:07,110
Oh, when I'm up here,

761
00:44:07,110 --> 00:44:08,970
I don't even feel the cold.

762
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:10,340
I just feel...

763
00:44:10,340 --> 00:44:12,680
Free.

764
00:44:15,420 --> 00:44:17,380
This is what it is

765
00:44:17,380 --> 00:44:20,650
to be a dragon, hiccup.

766
00:44:20,650 --> 00:44:22,720
It's all well and good

767
00:44:22,720 --> 00:44:23,960
to call yourself a dragon,

768
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:25,190
but can you fly?

769
00:44:46,780 --> 00:44:48,250
Oh, no! Aah!

770
00:44:58,760 --> 00:45:00,430
Man, almost!

771
00:45:00,430 --> 00:45:02,760
We just about had it that time.

772
00:45:08,030 --> 00:45:09,300
Incredible.

773
00:45:09,300 --> 00:45:11,740
Well, not bad yourself.

774
00:45:22,250 --> 00:45:25,820
All this time, you took after me.

775
00:45:25,820 --> 00:45:27,720
And...

776
00:45:27,720 --> 00:45:29,490
Where was I?

777
00:45:30,720 --> 00:45:32,990
I'm so sorry, hiccup.

778
00:45:32,990 --> 00:45:35,960
Can we start over?

779
00:45:39,130 --> 00:45:41,900
Will you give me another chance?

780
00:45:44,370 --> 00:45:46,900
I-I can teach you all that I've learned

781
00:45:46,910 --> 00:45:49,910
these past 20 years.

782
00:45:49,910 --> 00:45:51,410
Like...

783
00:45:55,880 --> 00:45:57,050
Wow.

784
00:45:57,050 --> 00:45:59,320
Now you can make those tight turns.

785
00:46:01,220 --> 00:46:03,490
Did you know about this?

786
00:46:03,490 --> 00:46:06,090
Every dragon

787
00:46:06,090 --> 00:46:08,330
has its secrets. And...

788
00:46:08,330 --> 00:46:10,360
I'll show them all to you.

789
00:46:10,360 --> 00:46:12,900
We'll unlock every mystery,

790
00:46:12,900 --> 00:46:15,970
find every last species-- together, as mother and son.

791
00:46:22,540 --> 00:46:24,980
This gift we share, hiccup,

792
00:46:24,980 --> 00:46:26,980
it bonds us.

793
00:46:26,980 --> 00:46:31,080
This is who you are, son.

794
00:46:31,080 --> 00:46:32,850
Who we are.

795
00:46:32,850 --> 00:46:36,490
We will change the world for all dragons.

796
00:46:36,490 --> 00:46:39,290
We will make it a better, safer place.

797
00:46:39,290 --> 00:46:40,890
Yeah, I mean,

798
00:46:40,890 --> 00:46:43,330
that sounds amazing.

799
00:46:55,340 --> 00:46:57,380
Oh, this is so great!

800
00:46:57,380 --> 00:47:00,580
Now you and I can go talk to drago together.

801
00:47:00,580 --> 00:47:02,050
: What?

802
00:47:02,050 --> 00:47:04,380
There's no talking to drago.

803
00:47:04,380 --> 00:47:05,880
- But we have to... - No.

804
00:47:05,890 --> 00:47:08,150
We must protect our own.

805
00:47:08,150 --> 00:47:09,250
Come on.

806
00:47:09,260 --> 00:47:10,590
We should be getting back.

807
00:47:10,590 --> 00:47:12,560
Hmm?

808
00:47:25,500 --> 00:47:27,870
Okay, I got you here!

809
00:47:27,870 --> 00:47:29,210
Now get this thing off me.

810
00:47:29,210 --> 00:47:31,010
Never take a toy from a dragon.

811
00:47:31,010 --> 00:47:32,510
Don't you know anything?

812
00:47:33,980 --> 00:47:36,410
Why does this keep happening to me?

813
00:47:50,900 --> 00:47:52,360
What's down there?

814
00:47:54,230 --> 00:47:55,500
Large diameter bubbles,

815
00:47:55,500 --> 00:47:57,270
massive lungs,

816
00:47:57,270 --> 00:47:59,500
cold water deep dweller, I'm thinking

817
00:47:59,510 --> 00:48:01,510
class five leviathan,

818
00:48:01,510 --> 00:48:03,140
maybe six.

819
00:48:06,610 --> 00:48:08,480
Eret: Yah!

820
00:48:17,990 --> 00:48:19,520
Meatlug, what's wrong, girl? Hookfang! Come on!

821
00:48:19,530 --> 00:48:21,090
Don't move!

822
00:48:21,090 --> 00:48:22,560
Uh...

823
00:48:36,910 --> 00:48:38,480
Drago!

824
00:48:43,080 --> 00:48:45,020
Get off me!

825
00:48:46,290 --> 00:48:48,490
Always great to see you, my friend.

826
00:48:48,490 --> 00:48:50,620
Keeping warm up here?

827
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:56,690
Well, as you can see, I am right on time

828
00:48:56,700 --> 00:48:58,630
with a new batch of dragons,

829
00:48:58,630 --> 00:49:00,030
just like I promised.

830
00:49:00,030 --> 00:49:01,630
He's waking up! Drop the ropes!

831
00:49:01,630 --> 00:49:03,200
Give me some backup here!

832
00:49:03,200 --> 00:49:04,700
Watch out!

833
00:49:04,700 --> 00:49:06,300
Drop the ropes.

834
00:49:39,200 --> 00:49:41,070
Hookfang! Ruffnut: Hey!

835
00:49:41,070 --> 00:49:42,410
What are you doing?!

836
00:49:42,410 --> 00:49:44,180
You belong

837
00:49:44,180 --> 00:49:46,080
to me now.

838
00:49:47,350 --> 00:49:49,510
And as an added bonus,

839
00:49:49,520 --> 00:49:52,120
I also caught you their riders.

840
00:49:52,120 --> 00:49:54,120
