1119
01:07:59,200 --> 01:08:00,440
Stop!

1120
01:08:02,570 --> 01:08:03,840
Stop!

1121
01:08:09,680 --> 01:08:13,720
This... Is the great dragon master?

1122
01:08:13,720 --> 01:08:16,250
The son of stoick the vast?

1123
01:08:17,720 --> 01:08:21,560
What shame he must feel.

1124
01:08:21,560 --> 01:08:24,290
All of this loss...

1125
01:08:24,300 --> 01:08:25,830
And for what?

1126
01:08:25,830 --> 01:08:27,800
To become unstoppable?

1127
01:08:27,800 --> 01:08:30,230
To rule the world?

1128
01:08:30,240 --> 01:08:33,600
Dragons, they-they are kind, amazing creatures

1129
01:08:33,610 --> 01:08:35,810
that can bring people together.

1130
01:08:37,740 --> 01:08:40,810
Or tear them apart.

1131
01:08:42,550 --> 01:08:45,250
You see, I know what it is

1132
01:08:45,250 --> 01:08:47,750
to live in fear,

1133
01:08:47,750 --> 01:08:50,590
to see my village burned,

1134
01:08:50,590 --> 01:08:53,620
my family taken.

1135
01:08:53,630 --> 01:08:56,360
But even as a boy...

1136
01:08:56,360 --> 01:08:58,560
Left with nothing,

1137
01:08:58,560 --> 01:09:00,730
I vowed to rise above

1138
01:09:00,730 --> 01:09:03,370
the fear of dragons...

1139
01:09:04,770 --> 01:09:08,140
...and liberate the people of this world.

1140
01:09:08,140 --> 01:09:10,440
Then why a dragon army?

1141
01:09:10,440 --> 01:09:14,840
Well, you need dragons to conquer other dragons.

1142
01:09:14,850 --> 01:09:18,250
Or maybe you need dragons to conquer people...

1143
01:09:18,250 --> 01:09:21,150
To control those who follow you...

1144
01:09:21,150 --> 01:09:23,620
And to get rid of those who won't.

1145
01:09:26,220 --> 01:09:28,490
Clever boy.

1146
01:09:28,490 --> 01:09:30,930
The world wants peace,

1147
01:09:30,930 --> 01:09:34,260
and we have the answer back on berk.

1148
01:09:34,270 --> 01:09:36,400
Just... let me show you--

1149
01:09:36,400 --> 01:09:38,470
no!

1150
01:09:38,470 --> 01:09:40,240
Let me...

1151
01:09:40,240 --> 01:09:42,270
Show you!

1152
01:09:49,920 --> 01:09:50,910
What in...

1153
01:09:55,720 --> 01:09:57,890
Hiccup!

1154
01:09:57,890 --> 01:10:00,360
Come on, gobber!

1155
01:10:00,360 --> 01:10:02,830
Okay, change of plan.

1156
01:10:04,900 --> 01:10:08,630
No dragon can resist the Alpha's command.

1157
01:10:08,630 --> 01:10:12,670
So he who controls the Alpha...

1158
01:10:12,670 --> 01:10:15,970
Controls them all.

1159
01:10:18,440 --> 01:10:20,810
Toothless?

1160
01:10:26,220 --> 01:10:28,590
T-toothless, you okay, bud? What's going on?

1161
01:10:28,590 --> 01:10:30,450
Witness true strength.

1162
01:10:32,590 --> 01:10:35,660
The strength of will over others.

1163
01:10:40,500 --> 01:10:42,230
In the face of it,

1164
01:10:42,230 --> 01:10:45,600
you are nothing.

1165
01:10:49,710 --> 01:10:52,440
Uh... what did he just tell you?

1166
01:10:56,250 --> 01:10:57,750
Toothless, come on.

1167
01:10:57,750 --> 01:10:59,550
What's the matter with you?

1168
01:10:59,550 --> 01:11:01,350
No, no, no, no, come on, what are you doing?

1169
01:11:01,350 --> 01:11:02,750
Knock it off.

1170
01:11:02,750 --> 01:11:05,260
: Stop! Snap out of it!

1171
01:11:11,700 --> 01:11:13,530
Toothless, no!

1172
01:11:13,530 --> 01:11:15,500
Toothless!

1173
01:11:19,400 --> 01:11:20,870
- Don't! - Hiccup!

1174
01:11:22,370 --> 01:11:24,510
- Stop...! - Son!

1175
01:11:24,510 --> 01:11:25,510
Dad!

1176
01:11:25,510 --> 01:11:26,780
No!

1177
01:11:33,450 --> 01:11:34,580
Hmm.

1178
01:11:45,760 --> 01:11:47,660
No...

1179
01:11:54,970 --> 01:11:56,640
Dad!

1180
01:11:56,640 --> 01:11:58,640
Stoick...

1181
01:12:01,810 --> 01:12:03,380
Dad?

1182
01:12:03,380 --> 01:12:05,620
No. You...

1183
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:19,460
No.

1184
01:12:28,710 --> 01:12:30,510
No, no, no. No.

1185
01:12:51,860 --> 01:12:54,130
No! Get away from him!

1186
01:12:56,000 --> 01:12:57,630
Go on! Get out of here!

1187
01:12:57,640 --> 01:13:00,470
Get away!

1188
01:13:00,470 --> 01:13:03,440
Valka: It's not his fault.

1189
01:13:03,440 --> 01:13:05,740
You know that.

1190
01:13:10,650 --> 01:13:12,720
Good dragons

1191
01:13:12,720 --> 01:13:14,580
under the control of bad people...

1192
01:13:14,590 --> 01:13:18,020
No, wait. Don't go. ...Do bad things.

1193
01:13:37,910 --> 01:13:40,580
Come on!

1194
01:13:40,580 --> 01:13:42,910
Gather the men and meet me at berk!

1195
01:13:42,910 --> 01:13:46,480
Toothless! No, don't.

1196
01:14:11,810 --> 01:14:14,540
May the valkyries welcome you

1197
01:14:14,550 --> 01:14:17,580
and lead you through odin's great battlefield.

1198
01:14:17,580 --> 01:14:20,850
May they sing your name with love and fury,

1199
01:14:20,850 --> 01:14:24,820
so that we might hear it rise from the depths of Valhalla,

1200
01:14:24,820 --> 01:14:27,690
and know that you've taken your rightful place

1201
01:14:27,690 --> 01:14:31,590
at the table of kings.

1202
01:14:31,600 --> 01:14:33,860
For a great man has fallen.

1203
01:14:33,870 --> 01:14:35,500
A warrior.

1204
01:14:36,600 --> 01:14:38,600
A chieftain.

1205
01:14:38,600 --> 01:14:40,540
A father.

1206
01:14:41,610 --> 01:14:43,840
A friend.

1207
01:15:17,240 --> 01:15:20,740
I'm sorry, dad.

1208
01:15:31,790 --> 01:15:34,060
I'm not the chief that...

1209
01:15:34,060 --> 01:15:36,230
You wanted me to be.

1210
01:15:36,230 --> 01:15:39,800
And I'm not the peacekeeper I thought I was.

1211
01:15:41,900 --> 01:15:45,030
I... don't know...

1212
01:15:57,180 --> 01:16:00,180
You came early into this world.

1213
01:16:00,180 --> 01:16:02,820
You were such a wee thing.

1214
01:16:02,820 --> 01:16:06,320
Oh, so frail, so fragile.

1215
01:16:06,320 --> 01:16:08,890
I feared you wouldn't make it.

1216
01:16:10,690 --> 01:16:13,260
But your father...

1217
01:16:13,260 --> 01:16:16,070
He never doubted.

1218
01:16:16,070 --> 01:16:20,340
He always said you'd become the strongest of them all.

1219
01:16:20,340 --> 01:16:22,640
And he was right.

1220
01:16:23,870 --> 01:16:26,810
You have the heart of a chief,

1221
01:16:26,810 --> 01:16:29,250
and the soul of a dragon.

1222
01:16:29,250 --> 01:16:33,980
Only you can bring our worlds together.

1223
01:16:33,990 --> 01:16:38,050
That... is who you are, son.

1224
01:16:51,600 --> 01:16:53,970
I, uh...

1225
01:16:53,970 --> 01:16:57,110
I was so afraid of becoming my dad.

1226
01:16:58,380 --> 01:17:02,040
Mostly because I thought I never could.

1227
01:17:02,050 --> 01:17:05,110
How-how do you become someone...

1228
01:17:05,120 --> 01:17:07,720
That great, that... brave,

1229
01:17:07,720 --> 01:17:10,220
that... selfless?

1230
01:17:13,320 --> 01:17:16,290
I guess you can only try.

1231
01:17:23,700 --> 01:17:26,800
A chief protects his own.

1232
01:17:29,670 --> 01:17:31,340
We're going back.

1233
01:17:32,980 --> 01:17:36,980
Uh... with what? Uh, he took all the dragons.

1234
01:17:36,980 --> 01:17:39,350
Not all of them.

1235
01:17:43,090 --> 01:17:44,420
Whoa!

1236
01:17:44,420 --> 01:17:47,760
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

1237
01:17:50,090 --> 01:17:51,390
I don't want to die!

1238
01:17:51,400 --> 01:17:53,660
We can't fly things!

1239
01:17:53,670 --> 01:17:54,830
Yeah, no kidding!

1240
01:17:54,830 --> 01:17:56,830
Whoa...!

1241
01:17:58,300 --> 01:18:00,040
But won't that bewilderbeast

1242
01:18:00,040 --> 01:18:02,810
just take control of these guys, too?

1243
01:18:02,810 --> 01:18:05,710
: They're babies! They don't listen to anyone.

1244
01:18:05,710 --> 01:18:07,840
Yeah. Just like us.

1245
01:18:07,850 --> 01:18:10,410
This is-- whoa!-- Very dangerous!

1246
01:18:14,050 --> 01:18:16,420
Some might suggest

1247
01:18:16,420 --> 01:18:19,020
this is poorly conceived!

1248
01:18:19,020 --> 01:18:21,060
Well, it's a good thing that I never listen.

1249
01:18:21,060 --> 01:18:22,460
Whoa!

1250
01:18:22,460 --> 01:18:23,890
So...

1251
01:18:23,900 --> 01:18:24,890
What is your...

1252
01:18:24,900 --> 01:18:26,260
Plan?

1253
01:18:26,260 --> 01:18:29,230
Get toothless back and kick drago's...

1254
01:18:29,230 --> 01:18:31,070
Heads up!

1255
01:18:31,070 --> 01:18:32,940
And that thing.

1256
01:18:32,940 --> 01:18:34,900
Whoa... ow!

1257
01:18:54,960 --> 01:18:56,430
Oh! Oh...

1258
01:18:56,430 --> 01:18:58,430
Ah, that's a good boy.

1259
01:19:02,870 --> 01:19:04,170
Uh...

1260
01:19:04,170 --> 01:19:06,100
W-w-watch the furniture!

1261
01:19:06,100 --> 01:19:08,240
Where are you going?

1262
01:19:25,790 --> 01:19:28,820
Your chief... is dead!

1263
01:19:28,830 --> 01:19:31,190
Stoick? No! Not possible!

1264
01:19:31,200 --> 01:19:33,800
No one can protect you now!

1265
01:19:48,080 --> 01:19:50,480
No.

1266
01:19:50,480 --> 01:19:54,280
He took all the dragons.

1267
01:19:54,290 --> 01:19:55,920
Distract the Alpha.

1268
01:19:55,920 --> 01:19:58,390
Try to keep his focus off of toothless.

1269
01:19:58,390 --> 01:19:59,890
Uh, how?

1270
01:19:59,890 --> 01:20:02,060
Have you forgotten who you're riding with?

1271
01:20:02,060 --> 01:20:05,490
There isn't a dragon alive that I can't wrangle! Aah!

1272
01:20:05,500 --> 01:20:08,560
Except for this one...! Snotlout : Amateur.

1273
01:20:08,570 --> 01:20:11,030
Hey, look! It's hiccup!

1274
01:20:16,570 --> 01:20:19,510
What?

1275
01:20:32,960 --> 01:20:34,590
Ruffnut : Keep 'em coming!

1276
01:20:34,590 --> 01:20:36,290
Black sheep, baby!

1277
01:20:46,600 --> 01:20:48,470
Ten points!

1278
01:20:50,240 --> 01:20:52,010
Uh-oh.

1279
01:21:02,620 --> 01:21:04,590
I'm okay!

1280
01:21:12,100 --> 01:21:15,500
You certainly are hard to get rid of, I'll say that.

1281
01:21:15,500 --> 01:21:17,500
Toothless...

1282
01:21:17,500 --> 01:21:19,500
Hey.

1283
01:21:19,500 --> 01:21:21,600
: It's me, bud.

1284
01:21:21,610 --> 01:21:23,110
It's me.

1285
01:21:23,110 --> 01:21:25,170
It's me. I'm right here, bud.

1286
01:21:25,180 --> 01:21:27,080
Come back to me.

1287
01:21:29,010 --> 01:21:31,650
He's not yours anymore.

1288
01:21:31,650 --> 01:21:34,050
He belongs to the Alpha.

1289
01:21:34,050 --> 01:21:37,520
But, please, o great dragon master,

1290
01:21:37,520 --> 01:21:40,160
try... to take him.

1291
01:21:40,160 --> 01:21:43,590
He will not miss a second time.

1292
01:21:43,590 --> 01:21:45,930
It wasn't your fault, bud.

1293
01:21:47,300 --> 01:21:49,670
They... made you do it.

1294
01:21:59,180 --> 01:22:01,510
You'd never hurt him.

1295
01:22:05,250 --> 01:22:08,480
You'd never hurt me.

1296
01:22:11,690 --> 01:22:13,660
How are you doing that?

1297
01:22:13,660 --> 01:22:17,160
Please. You are my best friend, bud.

1298
01:22:21,300 --> 01:22:23,200
My best friend.

1299
01:22:28,040 --> 01:22:30,440
Attaboy! That's it!

1300
01:22:30,440 --> 01:22:31,470
I'm here.

1301
01:22:31,480 --> 01:22:33,180
Enough!

1302
01:22:37,720 --> 01:22:39,010
Yeah!

1303
01:22:39,020 --> 01:22:41,120
Hang on!

1304
01:22:45,590 --> 01:22:47,420
Almost there, buddy, almost there.

1305
01:22:56,570 --> 01:22:59,070
Do something!

1306
01:22:59,070 --> 01:23:01,040
We need to get those two apart.

1307
01:23:11,280 --> 01:23:13,750
We gotta block him out, toothless.

1308
01:23:13,750 --> 01:23:15,580
Do you trust me, bud?

1309
01:23:17,690 --> 01:23:19,490
We can do this.

1310
01:23:19,490 --> 01:23:22,260
You... and me...

1311
01:23:22,260 --> 01:23:23,990
As one.

1312
01:23:26,000 --> 01:23:27,760
That's it.

1313
01:23:27,770 --> 01:23:31,100
Now let's try this one more time!

1314
01:23:31,100 --> 01:23:34,200
Astrid: Take him down, babe!

1315
01:23:37,670 --> 01:23:38,740
Go get him.

1316
01:23:41,210 --> 01:23:42,580
Take control of it!

1317
01:23:45,250 --> 01:23:46,520
Shut it out, toothless.

1318
01:23:46,520 --> 01:23:48,150
Stop them! Now!

1319
01:23:52,790 --> 01:23:54,620
Huh...?

1320
01:24:11,470 --> 01:24:12,510
Not again.

1321
01:24:14,680 --> 01:24:17,750
Toothless, it's now or never!

1322
01:24:19,680 --> 01:24:21,150
Come on, bud!

1323
01:24:23,350 --> 01:24:24,390
Hold on!

1324
01:24:27,560 --> 01:24:29,830
Ya-ha! We did it!

1325
01:24:38,100 --> 01:24:40,640
Hold him there, toothless.

1326
01:24:40,640 --> 01:24:42,770
It's all over now.

1327
01:24:44,440 --> 01:24:46,080
Or is it?

1328
01:24:46,840 --> 01:24:48,710
Uh...

1329
01:24:48,710 --> 01:24:50,150
Oh, no!

1330
01:24:58,860 --> 01:25:00,590
No!

1331
01:25:00,590 --> 01:25:03,560
No!

1332
01:25:11,400 --> 01:25:12,530
Hiccup...

1333
01:25:43,670 --> 01:25:45,230
He's challenging the Alpha!

1334
01:25:45,240 --> 01:25:46,770
To protect you!

1335
01:26:12,560 --> 01:26:15,660
No, no, no, no, no! No!

1336
01:26:15,670 --> 01:26:17,670
Fight back! Fight!

1337
01:26:17,670 --> 01:26:18,870
Fight!

1338
01:26:21,440 --> 01:26:23,770
What's the matter with you!

1339
01:26:26,940 --> 01:26:30,780
Hold your ground! Hold the line now!

1340
01:26:33,220 --> 01:26:35,280
Now do you get it?

1341
01:26:35,290 --> 01:26:38,820
This is what it is to earn a dragon's loyalty.

1342
01:26:40,790 --> 01:26:42,620
Let this end now.

1343
01:26:42,630 --> 01:26:43,860
Never!

1344
01:26:43,860 --> 01:26:45,230
Come on!

1345
01:26:53,240 --> 01:26:54,770
Huh?

1346
01:27:08,320 --> 01:27:09,750
Fight!

1347
01:27:43,350 --> 01:27:45,820
The Alpha... protects them all.

1348
01:28:45,350 --> 01:28:48,480
You never cease to amaze me, bud.

1349
01:28:48,490 --> 01:28:51,650
Thank you.

1350
01:28:53,320 --> 01:28:56,360
Toothless, you know that doesn't wash out!

1351
01:28:57,860 --> 01:29:00,700
I knew you'd come back! You're back, my beauty!

1352
01:29:00,700 --> 01:29:02,030
Oh! Oh!

1353
01:29:02,030 --> 01:29:04,470
Stormfly!

1354
01:29:07,500 --> 01:29:10,040
Oh, give me a cuddle, grumpy!

1355
01:29:10,040 --> 01:29:11,670
Oh!

1356
01:29:13,610 --> 01:29:15,110
Who's my little princess!

1357
01:29:15,110 --> 01:29:16,810
Don't you ever leave again, hookfang.

1358
01:29:16,810 --> 01:29:19,750
Oh, you are. Yes, you are. I missed you...

1359
01:29:19,750 --> 01:29:20,980
Oh, barf...

1360
01:29:20,980 --> 01:29:22,780
Not you!

1361
01:29:24,420 --> 01:29:26,520
That was some

1362
01:29:26,520 --> 01:29:28,660
pretty fine dragon- wrangling back there.

1363
01:29:28,660 --> 01:29:30,390
You'd make a good trapper.

1364
01:29:30,390 --> 01:29:31,860
Whoa.

1365
01:29:31,860 --> 01:29:34,500
You know... skullcrusher is gonna need somebody

1366
01:29:34,500 --> 01:29:36,370
to look after him now.

1367
01:29:36,370 --> 01:29:37,900
Me?

1368
01:29:41,500 --> 01:29:43,470
I'd be honored.

1369
01:29:44,510 --> 01:29:46,610
Oh, your father,

1370
01:29:46,610 --> 01:29:48,980
he'd be every bit as proud as I am.

1371
01:29:48,980 --> 01:29:50,850
Thank you.

1372
01:29:50,850 --> 01:29:52,950
I'm really glad you're here, mom.

1373
01:29:52,950 --> 01:29:55,020
And here I'll stay.

1374
01:29:56,550 --> 01:29:58,550
See?

1375
01:29:58,560 --> 01:30:00,020
I told you it was in here.

1376
01:30:00,020 --> 01:30:02,020
Ah, ha, ha.

1377
01:30:02,030 --> 01:30:03,760
You're still doing that one.

1378
01:30:03,760 --> 01:30:05,530
That's hilarious.

1379
01:30:05,530 --> 01:30:08,030
Come here, you. Mm!

1380
01:30:08,030 --> 01:30:10,130
Ooh!

1381
01:30:38,800 --> 01:30:41,830
the chief has come home!

1382
01:30:45,600 --> 01:30:46,940
Yeah!

1383
01:30:48,540 --> 01:30:50,710
Villagers : Long live the chief!

1384
01:30:50,710 --> 01:30:54,980
Long live the chief! Long live the chief!

1385
01:30:54,980 --> 01:30:57,150
Long live the chief!

1386
01:31:07,760 --> 01:31:09,520
Yeah! Ha-ha!

1387
01:31:11,160 --> 01:31:12,660
Ah...

1388
01:31:12,660 --> 01:31:15,930
Yah-ha-ha-ha!

1389
01:31:19,840 --> 01:31:21,970
This... is berk.

1390
01:31:21,970 --> 01:31:24,570
A bit trampled and busted

1391
01:31:24,580 --> 01:31:27,110
and covered in ice, but it's home.

1392
01:31:27,110 --> 01:31:29,510
It's our home.

1393
01:31:31,950 --> 01:31:33,720
Those who attacked us

1394
01:31:33,720 --> 01:31:35,820
are relentless and crazy.

1395
01:31:35,820 --> 01:31:38,690
But those who stopped them?

1396
01:31:38,690 --> 01:31:41,260
Oh... even more so!

1397
01:31:43,630 --> 01:31:47,130
We may be small in numbers, but we stand for something

1398
